    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #44748.\n\nGrayscale JPEGs decoded on GPU via `torchvision.io.decode_jpeg` (default unchanged mode) come back as `[1, H, W]`. `BaseMultimodalProcessor._load_single_item` returned those tensors unchanged, so Qwen-VL (and similar) processors that normalize with three RGB channel means fail:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: output with shape [1, 1, H, W] doesn't match the broadcast shape [1, 3, H, W]\n```\n\nRelated: #35101 forces `ImageReadMode.RGB` at the decode call site. This PR is defense in depth at the load boundary so any 1-channel tensor is expanded before processing, including when the decode path is unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `ensure_rgb_image_tensor` and use it from `smart_to_rgb` for tensors.\n- Route GPU-decoded tensors through `smart_to_rgb` in `_load_single_item` instead of returning them raw.\n- Add unit tests that mock `load_image` returning 1-channel / HW / RGB tensors.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- New unit tests in `test_base_processor_image_decode.py` (`TestLoadSingleItemGrayscaleGpuTensor`).\n- Helper smoke-checked for CHW `[1,H,W]` → `[3,H,W]`, HW → `[3,H,W]`, and RGB passthrough.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Style Guide](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#style-guide).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38992314098](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38992314098)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38992314180](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38992314180)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38992314113](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38992314113)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
